0 1 57 34 0 3 Fitting a Spectrum to the Filter
.TXT 48 2 120 0
Cg a66.125000,66.000000,421
{\rtf1\ansi \deff0
{\fonttbl
{\f0\fnil Arial;}
{\f1\fnil Symbol;}
}
{\plain Exercise   Notice that we chose 
a sampling frequency ten times greater than
 the Nyquist frequency in order to fit the
 signal spectrum into the region where the
 simple FIR filter worked reasonably well.
 A consequence is the need to process a 
lot of samples. We might try designing a
 more sophisticated filter to decrease the
 required sampling rate- but, very likely,
 at the cost of more computation per filter
 output!}
}
